WEBVTT

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:04.220
- Can I help you? - I'd like to see the man in charge.

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:06.730
He's in here.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:23.170
Sit down. Who was this murder committed?

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:27.430
- San Francisco, last night. - Who was murdered?

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:41.970
You want to hear me out, or don't you, Captain?

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.510
I don't have very much time.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.110
Your name Bigelow?

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.110
Frank Bigelow?

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:55.630
Answer the San Francisco APB.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:57.920
Send it direct to Inspector Bannon at Homicide.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.000
Tell him we found Frank Bigelow.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:08.930
- Go ahead, Mr. Bigelow. - This involves some other people, Captain.

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:12.360
- A number of other people. - You tell it any way you like.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:18.880
I live in a little town called Banning, out in the desert.

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:25.470
It's on the way to Palm Springs. I have a small business there.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:28.900
Paula.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:35.020
- Yes, Mr. Bigelow. - Give me a copy of Miss Hollis' 48 tax return, will you?

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.770
- Oh, you'd better get the 47, too. - Yes, Mr. Bigelow.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.490
I don't think we took any depreciation on that new equipment last year.

00:03:42.690 --> 00:03:46.090
No, we didn't. I remember you said we could include it all this year.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:48.660
- Sure, we can. - Hey, Frank.

00:03:48.840 --> 00:03:52.310
Peterson says he wants a financial statement before he can give me my loan.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.680
- Hello, Kitty. - Hi, Will.

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:56.450
I'm leaving for San Francisco today, but I'll be back in about a week.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:57.850
I'll take care of it for you then.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.000
- Sure is a scorcher, isn't it? - Well, I've seen him worried.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.850
- Have a nice time, Frank. - Thanks, Will.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:05.060
Why don't you come down to the place and let me give you another permanent.

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:08.270
It makes your hair so much easier to manage in all this heat.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:11.260
I can't afford it right now. Maybe next month.

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.300
Here it is. No, we didn't take it. Well, we can do it this year.

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:18.100
You work it out any way you think best. Have a nice trip, Frank.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.100
Sure, Kitty. See you when I get back.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:25.210
Bon voyage. Why don't you come down anyway, Paula?

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:28.160
We'll work out a deal on that permanent.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.000
Thanks. Maybe I will.

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:36.920
- Hello? - Hello, Mr. Hawkins.

00:04:37.670 --> 00:04:41.200
- Do you want him to send your ticket over? - No, I'll pick it up.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:43.800
No, no, Mr. Bigelow will pick it up at the station.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:51.190
- Bye. - I want to go with you, Frank.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.400
I'm just going on a little vacation, you know that.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.170
- You want to go without me, don't you? - I'll be gone in just a week.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:00.000
And I suppose you've just made up your mind to take this little vacation

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.400
at 9:00 this morning?

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:04.000
No, Paula, I meant to tell you about it a few days ago.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:06.120
- I guess I forgot. - Oh, you forgot.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:09.240
- Paula, don't be like that. - Don't be like what?

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.560
You just drop a little announcement that you're going away.

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.960
Not tomorrow, or next week, or next month, but today.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:15.360
No explanations, nothing.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.760
And I'm supposed to swallow the excuse that you need a little vacation.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:22.000
I just want to get away from town for a few days, that's all.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.000
Get away from this town or get away from me.

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:26.880
Oh, Paula, please try to understand.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:29.290
How can you ask me to understand anything like this?

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.000
No, I'm sorry.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.260
I'm sorry, but I don't understand.

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:39.760
Go to San Francisco, but don't expect me to be waiting for you when you get back.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:10.950
Why do you do this to me, Frank?

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:12.860
Why can't you be honest with me?

00:06:13.060 --> 00:06:14.600
As honest as I am with you?

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.100
- Do you have to go? - I have to go, Paula.

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:19.100
- I know what I'm doing. - All right, go.

00:06:19.300 --> 00:06:21.700
Go anywhere you like. You can go to blazes for all I care.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:30.000
- Paula? - Yes, I know. I'm being fooled.

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:44.950
We'll go to Eddie's and have a drink.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:47.000
Why not?

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.860
A couple of cold beers, will you?

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:58.320
All right.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:06.550
Oh, my relief. This air-conditioning feels good.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:09.390
I wish we had it in the office. It would make it a pleasure.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:12.100
If it stays this hot, don't bother going in the rest of the week.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:14.960
- I won two races today. - How many did you lose?

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:16.360
You'd have to ask that.

00:07:17.320 --> 00:07:18.520
It's early for you two, isn't it?

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:20.680
It's too hot to work. That's what I'd like to hear.

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.270
You'll take me with you, won't you?

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:47.350
You will, won't you?

00:07:49.470 --> 00:07:50.640
Or am I crowding you?

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:52.980
What do you mean?

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:57.560
Maybe you need to be alone this week.

00:07:58.820 --> 00:07:59.890
Maybe we both do.

00:08:01.020 --> 00:08:03.080
I know what's going on inside of you, Frank.

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:05.410
You're just like any other man, but a little more so.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.640
You have a feeling of being trapped,

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.960
and you don't know whether or not you like it.

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:13.030
Look, Paula, I'm going to be honest with you.

00:08:13.170 --> 00:08:15.060
I care too much for you not to be honest with you.

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:18.170
I'm as much concerned for your happiness as I am for my own.

00:08:18.370 --> 00:08:20.770
I know you've had one bad experience, Frank. I know all about it.

00:08:20.970 --> 00:08:23.010
But you don't know what it can do to two people, Paula.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:28.130
And the woman always gets hurt more than the man, darling.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:38.360
I don't want you to get hurt.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:48.260
This won't bother you, will it?

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.610
The next result won't come in for half an hour.

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:03.220
I thought that by now we'd be married.

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:08.200
No, I'm not going to crowd you anymore, Frank.

00:09:08.410 --> 00:09:09.490
Go to San Francisco.

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:12.770
I don't like it, but I'm convinced that you must go.

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:16.250
I want you to be very sure, Frank.

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:18.760
If it's right, and I believe it is,

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:21.320
we'll have something really wonderful together.

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:26.130
If it isn't, we should both know it as soon as possible.

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.000
So, you see, even if I could stop you,

00:09:30.120 --> 00:10:00.000
I wouldn't do it now.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:02.060
- My name's Bigelow. I have a reservation. - Yes, sir.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:10.270
- Here we are, sir. - My name's Bigelow. I have a reservation.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:13.270
I have it, sir. It's a very nice room on the sixth floor, facing the bay.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:13.930
Thank you.

00:10:13.930 --> 00:10:17.130
Boy, this might help you enjoy your stay, Mr. Bigelow.

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:20.010
It's a little booklet on how to have fun in San Francisco.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.920
- Oh, thank you. - Very welcome, sir.

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:27.380
- Thank you. - Say, is it always like this around here?

00:10:27.380 --> 00:10:30.000
No, this is market week, and it's the last day, too.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:33.750
- Boy! - Always around until you need him.

00:10:33.750 --> 00:10:38.800
- 517? - Thank you.

00:10:38.800 --> 00:10:40.530
Here's a message for you, Mr. Bigelow.

00:10:40.530 --> 00:10:44.530
Long-distance call came in about an hour ago from Banning, from a Paula Gibson.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:47.330
- Oh, thank you. - Very welcome. Show Mr. Bigelow to 618.

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:48.500
Right this way, sir.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:07.160
This way, Mr. Bigler.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:28.810
You can get me a hat and a razor blade.

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:30.000
Thank you.

00:11:30.510 --> 00:11:32.430
Oh, and, uh, you can leave that door open.

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:36.240
Hello, operator.

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:39.850
I want to speak to Miss Paula Gibson in Banning, California.

00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:40.880
Yeah, that's right.

00:11:41.420 --> 00:11:42.020
No, I'll wait.

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:47.160
Hello?

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:50.570
Oh, hello, Frank. How was the trip?

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:51.810
Fine, just fine.

00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:53.680
Having a miserable time, I hope.

00:11:54.130 --> 00:11:56.490
Well, I don't know. I, uh, I just got in.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:57.200
Ah!

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:03.760
Market Week. The place is crawling with traveling salesmen.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:07.150
You know, Charlie Anderson found out that you went away and asked me to go out with him.

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:09.700
Oh, really? How did he make out?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.170
I'm considering it.

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:13.030
Is that what you called to tell me?

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:16.390
I'll have you know that this call is strictly business, Mr. Bigelow.

00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:19.630
Did a Mr. Phillips phone you? A Eugene Phillips of Los Angeles?

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:20.070
No.

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:22.510
He will. He phoned the office three times today.

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.550
Said that he wanted to get in touch with you immediately.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:27.580
He said it's most urgent and imperative that he reach you at once.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:28.530
What'd he want?

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:30.000
I don't know.

00:12:31.530 --> 00:13:00.000
quite agitated about something. Phillips, Phillips, have we ever done any business with him? Not unless you've been keeping it a secret for me. I looked through all the accounts. Why did you tell him you could reach me here? You know I'm supposed to be on vacation. So you told me. And so I told him, dear heart. But the gentleman didn't seem to respect your temperamental moods the way I do. He was very insistent that he speak to you before it's too late, as he put it. Well, tell him you try to get in touch with me.

00:13:00.030 --> 00:13:02.270
I've changed my plans, and you can't reach me.

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:03.770
He won't talk to me.

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:06.070
I told him that I was your confidential secretary,

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:08.470
but I guess I didn't sound confidential enough.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:10.880
So I told him that he could reach you there this evening.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:11.680
Well, call him back.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:14.280
If it's as important as he says it is, he'll talk to you.

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:16.420
Otherwise, you'll just have to wait until I get home.

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:19.480
My, aren't we adamant this evening?

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:20.430
All right.

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:23.840
Shall do.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:24.890
And Frank...

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:26.570
Yeah?

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:28.330
I...

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:30.000
I don't quite know how to say this.

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:37.270
- What? - I want to say that you don't have to feel guilty about it.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.600
I'll call you tomorrow.

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:19.110
Just put it there.

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.340
- You can keep the change. - Thank you very much.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.400
How long has this been going on?

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:27.920
It's been a madhouse all week.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:29.600
- But they check out tomorrow. - Oh?

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.040
- I thought you were with him. - No, I'm just here on a vacation.

00:14:33.270 --> 00:14:35.910
Why does everyone come to San Francisco and tear loose?

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:39.570
Excuse me.

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:44.130
I'm sorry to bother you, but would you mind if I use your phone?

00:14:44.330 --> 00:14:46.370
- No, go ahead. - I'm Mr. Cross at the hall.

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:50.330
One of the boys is using my phone, and he's been on for half an hour.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:52.950
- I just want to call downstairs. - Thank you.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:55.930
Moon service, please.

00:14:56.770 --> 00:14:59.030
Things really picked up the last few days, didn't they?

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.000
You read it much business?

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:01.530
Well, I'm not here on business.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:02.950
Oh, hello, room service.

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:04.570
It's Mr. Haskell in 617.

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:05.370
Yes, that's right.

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:07.490
Would you send up three more bottles of bourbon

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:08.570
and two scotch?

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:10.290
Yes, that's right.

00:15:10.290 --> 00:15:12.570
Oh, and some more ice, too.

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.530
All right, thank you.

00:15:14.530 --> 00:15:15.570
You here all alone?

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:16.710
Yes, I just got in town.

00:15:16.710 --> 00:15:18.750
Well, why don't you join us for a drink?

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:20.320
Well, I don't want to budge in on your party.

00:15:20.320 --> 00:15:22.480
Oh, nonsense, it's not a party.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:24.160
Just a few of the boys entertaining some buyers.

00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:28.170
You know, the usual thing, a few drinks and some laughs.

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:30.000
It's no party, come on.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:32.060
Come on, come on, come on!

00:15:32.060 --> 00:15:34.860
I don't like to be all alone in a strange city.

00:15:34.860 --> 00:15:37.040
- I'm Sam Haskell. - I'm Frank...

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:38.580
Frank Bigelow.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.160
You think some of these guys have never been away from home before?

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:42.830
Yeah.

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:47.960
Hey, hey, can you quiet down a second?

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.660
- I want you to meet Frank Bigelow. - Hello.

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:51.960
- This is Jane Carlisle. - Hello.

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.160
- Bill Welch. - How are you?

00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:54.570
- Mr. Welch. - Glad to know you, Bigelow.

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:57.270
- Jane's the prettiest buyer in San Francisco. - Oh, hey!

00:15:57.270 --> 00:16:00.000
- I resent that. - You don't think I believe him, Elaine.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:01.930
You spread that from coast to coast.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:03.690
But it's good for my morale.

00:16:03.890 --> 00:16:04.930
I'm George Cantwell.

00:16:05.130 --> 00:16:07.490
I'm glad to know you, Mr. Bigelow.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:08.370
Do you have any business?

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:09.570
He's not here.

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:14.260
Why don't you get the man a drink before he dies at first?

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:15.810
- How about bourbon? - That's fine.

00:16:15.950 --> 00:16:16.610
Bourbon it is.

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:20.380
Of course, Mr. Wallace, Inspector.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:21.700
Yes, Mr. Wallace.

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:26.040
But I'll need at least a week in Cleveland to visit all my accounts.

00:16:26.240 --> 00:16:28.450
I can't figure out being in Philadelphia until the 17th.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.000
Eddie, will you get off the phone?

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.040
- I want you to meet Frank Biglow. - How are you?

00:16:32.040 --> 00:16:35.380
That's his boss. He's been trying for an hour to get his expense account boosted.

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:38.220
The way this guy holds on to a dollar, you'd think they weren't printing them anymore.

00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:41.490
Yes, Mr. Wallace. I'm leaving here the first thing in the morning.

00:16:41.490 --> 00:16:43.850
Yes, sir.

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:47.480
Oh, keep your hips loose, Harry. Like this.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:50.900
Oh, yeah. How's he doing?

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:52.360
Oh, there's nothing wrong with Harry's rubber.

00:16:52.360 --> 00:16:54.360
The two years ago, the Murray's wouldn't kill.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.290
Wait a minute. That was going all right, sir.

00:16:56.290 --> 00:16:57.790
This is Sue and Harry Brandtis.

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:00.000
Hello. Good to meet you. How are you?

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.000
Where did you find her, Sam, on a dance marathon?

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:04.000
She's marvellous.

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:06.270
Now that you could do the rumba.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:08.270
Well, a little, but I'm kind of rusty.

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:10.270
Anything would be an improvement after Harry.

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:12.270
How do you like that?

00:17:12.370 --> 00:17:14.510
Here it goes.

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:18.470
Hey, you're good.

00:17:18.570 --> 00:17:22.490
Oh, my wife, she's a good dancer, isn't she?

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:24.490
Oh, yeah.

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:29.080
Hey, fellas, I thought you were going to show us a good time tonight.

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:30.000
Is this doing the time?

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:34.170
That's right. We practically bankrupt our stores to buy everything you've got.

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:36.050
Then you keep us in this hotel room.

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:42.050
I agree. This is my last night to howl before I go back to being a dutiful housewife.

00:17:42.050 --> 00:17:44.050
Well, it looks like we're stuck, boys.

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:47.050
This is where we blow all our commissions in one night.

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:49.050
And you're coming with us, Bigelow.

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:52.050
Oh, no, thanks. You run along. I've got to get unpacked and have dinner.

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:54.050
Oh, no. You're not going to get away from me.

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:59.510
Now that I found a man who can dance, I'm going to hang on to him.

00:20:38.320 --> 00:20:39.180
- What would it be?

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:40.870
- Bourbon and water, no ice.

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:42.450
Nice, quiet place you got here.

00:20:42.450 --> 00:20:43.890
- Well, they hit the pitch in about an hour.

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:46.030
That's when they really go out of their minds.

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:49.910
- Who's the blonde?

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:51.670
- Oh, she's one of the chicks that hangs around here.

00:20:51.670 --> 00:20:53.450
She's jive crazy.

00:20:53.450 --> 00:20:54.490
- Come again?

00:20:54.490 --> 00:20:55.490
- Oh, you ain't hip, pal.

00:20:55.490 --> 00:20:57.580
Jive crazy means that she goes for this stuff.

00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:59.300
Just between you and me, I don't get it either,

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:00.000
but I gotta listen.

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:02.160
They're all connoisseurs, music lovers.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:03.920
Me, I like Guy Lombardo.

00:21:04.930 --> 00:21:06.030
What's the matter with him?

00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:08.590
Oh, he's flipped. The music's driving him crazy.

00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:10.450
Calm down, Jack.

00:21:10.790 --> 00:21:12.570
Oh, don't bother me, man. I'm being in life.

00:21:13.470 --> 00:21:14.830
Is the blonde alone?

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:17.850
Oh, sure. Society. She always comes in alone.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:20.450
Drives a big convertible, wears a mink coat,

00:21:20.650 --> 00:21:22.690
but knows everybody. But she always comes in alone.

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:30.000
I wanted to kiss you. I tried to...

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:33.260
What's your story, Jeanie?

00:21:33.260 --> 00:21:34.260
Easy.

00:21:34.260 --> 00:21:41.710
The fisherman.

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:42.710
That's really silk, isn't it?

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:43.710
Can I buy you a drink?

00:21:43.710 --> 00:21:44.710
Sure, thanks.

00:21:44.710 --> 00:21:46.720
Give me a blast, Leo.

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:50.050
Leo, I left my blast at the other end of the bar.

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:04.580
- My name's Jeannie. What's yours? - Frank.

00:22:05.350 --> 00:22:08.350
- I've never seen you here before, Frank. - Well, I've never been here.

00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:17.920
- This isn't mine. Mine was bourbon. - Well, sure it is. You saw me pour it.

00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:22.970
- Give me a fresh drink. - You think you say?

00:22:23.290 --> 00:22:26.600
Oh, listen to that piano. Feel those vibrations.

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:33.300
- You don't get the kicks out of this, do you? - I can live without it.

00:22:34.300 --> 00:22:37.390
- Why do you stay here? - I don't know.

00:22:37.390 --> 00:22:39.920
I bet I know. You're lonely in a big city.

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:53.260
You don't have to go into a routine with me. I like good company, too.

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:58.130
There are some people here I want to avoid. Couldn't we get out of here?

00:22:58.130 --> 00:23:00.000
Let me think about it.

00:23:00.280 --> 00:23:08.000
- How about going somewhere else then? - Why don't you meet me later?

00:23:08.000 --> 00:23:20.040
- Who? - I'll get that number later.

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:23.840
- It's my next stop. - They've got a band there that'll really fit.

00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:27.270
- See you, Jeannie. - Easy.

00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:54.420
mine, operator.

00:25:18.780 --> 00:25:19.780
Come on, sirs, please.

00:25:30.730 --> 00:25:31.580
I'm with you, waiter.

00:25:31.580 --> 00:25:34.780
Yes, sir.

00:25:34.780 --> 00:25:36.770
- Rest well, sir? - Yeah, sure.

00:25:36.770 --> 00:25:40.580
- May I? - Go ahead.

00:25:40.580 --> 00:25:43.980
- It's on there for you. - Thank you, sir.

00:25:43.980 --> 00:25:48.560
- Would you like anything else? - No, thank you, that's all.

00:25:48.560 --> 00:25:53.920
- Waiter. - Yes, sir?

00:25:53.920 --> 00:25:58.340
Take this away.

00:25:58.340 --> 00:25:59.960
Is there anything wrong, sir?

00:26:00.830 --> 00:26:03.190
Just take it away. I don't even want to look at it.

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:09.160
- Are you all right, sir? - Yeah, sure.

00:26:10.720 --> 00:26:13.080
I'm all right. I just had too big a night, I guess, that's all.

00:26:14.240 --> 00:26:17.120
- I need some fresh air. - Of course. Thank you, sir.

00:27:19.870 --> 00:27:23.540
Lung's in good condition, blood pressure normal, heart fine.

00:27:23.740 --> 00:27:26.600
Well, it's a good thing everybody isn't like you, Mr. Bigelow.

00:27:26.840 --> 00:27:30.000
- Put us doctors out of business. - I'm glad to hear it, doctor. I was a little worried.

00:27:30.060 --> 00:27:31.940
Don't let your belly ache worry.

00:27:32.020 --> 00:27:33.480
It could be just to change the climate.

00:27:33.560 --> 00:27:37.460
It's not an ache, Doctor. It's hard to describe the feeling.

00:27:37.680 --> 00:27:40.680
Maybe it was the drinks I had last night. I might have mixed them too much.

00:27:40.760 --> 00:27:44.250
Let's have another look at that throat.

00:27:46.250 --> 00:27:48.100
You may finish dressing now, Mr. Bigelow.

00:27:48.180 --> 00:27:50.260
I want to get the results of those tests we took.

00:27:50.340 --> 00:27:50.960
Thank you, Doctor.

00:28:13.400 --> 00:28:15.500
Mr. Bigelow, this is Dr. Schaefer.

00:28:15.680 --> 00:28:18.370
- Hello, Doctor, how are you? - Sit down, Mr. Bigelow.

00:28:19.730 --> 00:28:22.770
According to the information you gave Miss Wilson, you're not married, Mr. Bigelow.

00:28:22.930 --> 00:28:23.630
That's right.

00:28:23.790 --> 00:28:26.880
Do you have any relatives, family, anyone in San Francisco?

00:28:27.040 --> 00:28:30.000
No, no one. I don't know, a soul in San Francisco.

00:28:30.000 --> 00:28:34.540
- What is this, Doctor? Why all the questions? - You're a very sick man, Mr. Bigelow.

00:28:34.620 --> 00:28:37.030
Sick? But you told me I was in good shape.

00:28:37.110 --> 00:28:41.450
Yes, I know. But my preliminary examination didn't reveal your true condition.

00:28:41.520 --> 00:28:44.300
- You sound as if it's pretty serious, Doctor. - It's extremely serious.

00:28:44.380 --> 00:28:46.860
I want you to understand that we wouldn't tell you something like this

00:28:46.940 --> 00:28:49.620
- unless we were absolutely certain. - Of course, of course.

00:28:49.700 --> 00:28:52.020
You must steal yourself for a shock, Mr. Bigelow.

00:28:52.070 --> 00:28:54.260
Well, go on, Doctor. What is it you're trying to tell me?

00:28:54.340 --> 00:28:57.810
A test reveals the presence in your body of a luminous, toxic matter.

00:28:57.810 --> 00:28:59.440
What is that, exactly?

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:02.240
- Poison that attacks the vital organs. - Poison?

00:29:02.320 --> 00:29:04.520
We have no alternative but to tell you this.

00:29:04.600 --> 00:29:07.810
Your system has already absorbed sufficient toxin to prove fatal.

00:29:07.890 --> 00:29:10.560
I wish there was something that we could do.

00:29:10.970 --> 00:29:14.660
- What do you mean "wish"? You mean there's nothing... - There is nothing anyone can do.

00:29:14.740 --> 00:29:18.380
This is one of the few poisons of its type for which there is no antidote.

00:29:19.090 --> 00:29:22.150
This is fantastic! This is the most ridiculous thing...

00:29:22.670 --> 00:29:26.870
- You don't have very long. - What do you mean?

00:29:27.080 --> 00:29:30.000
A day, possibly a week, two weeks at the outside.

00:29:30.220 --> 00:29:31.650
It's hard to say exactly.

00:29:31.980 --> 00:29:33.740
This is impossible. I don't believe it.

00:29:33.820 --> 00:29:34.700
You've made a mistake.

00:29:34.780 --> 00:29:36.660
That's it. It could be a mistake, couldn't it?

00:29:36.740 --> 00:29:38.620
You have made a mistake, haven't you?

00:29:38.700 --> 00:29:41.100
Dr. Schaefer is an authority on toxicology.

00:29:41.180 --> 00:29:43.120
No mistake, Mr. Bigelow.

00:29:44.060 --> 00:29:45.710
Do you realize what you're saying?

00:29:46.030 --> 00:29:48.040
You're telling me that I'm dead.

00:29:48.340 --> 00:29:51.340
Do you think you can explain my life away in just a few words?

00:29:51.420 --> 00:29:53.580
I don't even know who you are. Why should I believe you?

00:29:53.660 --> 00:29:55.510
You must calm yourself, Mr. Bigelow.

00:29:55.640 --> 00:29:57.480
We want to offer you every assistance that we...

00:29:57.560 --> 00:30:00.000
Assistance? Who wants your assistance? Who wants anything from you?

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:01.280
you're nothing but a couple of phonies.

00:30:01.480 --> 00:30:02.440
Why, I think you're crazy.

00:30:02.680 --> 00:30:03.800
That's it. You're crazy.

00:30:03.880 --> 00:30:05.040
The both of you, you're crazy.

00:30:09.360 --> 00:30:22.640
Come on, tell me what?

00:30:23.760 --> 00:30:24.560
Get out of here, doctor.

00:30:26.050 --> 00:30:28.440
What's the matter with you?

00:30:28.520 --> 00:30:30.000
Doctor, I want you to examine.

00:30:30.540 --> 00:30:35.940
- It's poisonous. - I'm right in here.

00:30:38.210 --> 00:30:47.890
- You got it, all right. - Your system has already absorbed it.

00:30:49.250 --> 00:30:52.280
Are you sure, Doctor? Are you absolutely certain?

00:30:52.970 --> 00:30:59.860
- Couldn't there be some mistake? - It is.

00:31:00.350 --> 00:31:02.400
Toxin is actually luminous in the dark.

00:31:03.120 --> 00:31:04.870
Now, there's no doubt about it, Bigelow.

00:31:06.180 --> 00:31:10.150
I don't feel sick. My stomach is just a little bit upset.

00:31:10.370 --> 00:31:12.260
Maybe it's not as bad as you think, Doctor.

00:31:12.290 --> 00:31:13.410
That's characteristic.

00:31:13.930 --> 00:31:16.030
With a heavy jolt, you go suddenly in a matter of hours.

00:31:16.230 --> 00:31:19.360
But if the stuff is taken in a lesser degree, you last a while.

00:31:19.490 --> 00:31:24.270
And then, and then...

00:31:26.790 --> 00:31:28.590
Turn me straight, Doctor!

00:31:28.790 --> 00:31:30.000
Well, a number of things are involved.

00:31:30.250 --> 00:31:33.770
the systemic condition of the individual, the amount consumed...

00:31:33.930 --> 00:31:34.740
Yes.

00:31:35.500 --> 00:31:37.330
You won't feel too bad for a while.

00:31:37.730 --> 00:31:39.000
Then it will happen suddenly.

00:31:39.130 --> 00:31:42.070
A day, two days, a week at the most.

00:31:47.030 --> 00:31:50.100
A day? Two days?

00:31:50.280 --> 00:31:52.020
There's nothing that can be done now.

00:31:52.540 --> 00:31:54.710
If it had been caught in time, your stomach would have been washed out.

00:31:54.950 --> 00:31:56.760
But you've had it in you for some time now.

00:31:56.880 --> 00:31:58.480
For at least 12 hours, haven't you, Bigelow?

00:31:58.640 --> 00:31:59.600
I don't know.

00:32:00.830 --> 00:32:02.340
- You don't know? - No!

00:32:02.420 --> 00:32:04.080
- Don't you know how you got it? - No!

00:32:04.280 --> 00:32:05.400
This is no accident.

00:32:05.640 --> 00:32:07.200
Someone knew how to handle that.

00:32:07.260 --> 00:32:09.130
That wax is useless.

00:32:09.250 --> 00:32:11.690
The amount of alcohol in your body, you must have had it in liquor.

00:32:11.860 --> 00:32:13.360
I was drinking last night.

00:32:13.560 --> 00:32:15.750
I'll arrange for your admission to the hospital immediately.

00:32:16.370 --> 00:32:18.940
Of course, I'll have to notify the police.

00:32:19.420 --> 00:32:22.470
- This is a case for homicide. - Homicide?

00:32:22.620 --> 00:32:25.140
I don't think you understand, Bigelow.

00:32:26.100 --> 00:32:27.880
You've been murdered.

00:32:33.420 --> 00:32:34.740
Give me police headquarters, please.

00:32:35.800 --> 00:32:36.560
Homicide Bureau.

00:32:39.520 --> 00:32:40.020
Thank you.

00:35:50.800 --> 00:35:55.030
Open up. Open this door, I tell you.

00:35:55.420 --> 00:35:56.850
Open it up or I'll break it down.

00:35:57.730 --> 00:36:00.000
Where are those men? Where are those men who were here last night?

00:36:00.090 --> 00:36:01.770
I don't know that there are no men here.

00:36:01.850 --> 00:36:03.690
- Please go away. - Don't lie to me, where are they?

00:36:03.770 --> 00:36:06.210
Mister, this lady just checked in.

00:36:06.290 --> 00:36:07.850
Those men aren't here no longer.

00:36:07.930 --> 00:36:09.850
They checked out the hotel early this morning.

00:36:09.930 --> 00:36:12.180
- Checked out? - Please, go away.

00:36:12.580 --> 00:36:18.690
I'm sorry. I'm terribly sorry.

00:36:21.820 --> 00:36:25.980
- Hello? - Hello, my eardrums.

00:36:26.060 --> 00:36:27.260
Hello, Paula.

00:36:27.770 --> 00:36:30.000
Your enthusiasm overwhelms me.

00:36:30.860 --> 00:36:33.360
or is there a quota on telephone calls up there?

00:36:34.350 --> 00:36:36.950
I'm sorry, I've been busy.

00:36:37.400 --> 00:36:38.550
I'll bet you have.

00:36:38.750 --> 00:36:40.550
Visiting the museums, no doubt.

00:36:40.680 --> 00:36:43.000
What's happening up there that's exciting or different?

00:36:43.710 --> 00:36:45.330
Nothing, not a thing.

00:36:45.630 --> 00:36:47.960
I bet you miss me, but you're too stubborn to admit it.

00:36:48.500 --> 00:36:49.500
Sure, sure.

00:36:49.700 --> 00:36:52.500
You know, if you'd like me to come up, I can pack a toothbrush and leave right away.

00:36:52.700 --> 00:36:53.460
No!

00:36:54.360 --> 00:36:55.960
Well, you don't have to snap my head off.

00:36:56.160 --> 00:36:58.160
You could at least make a pretence of missing me.

00:36:59.280 --> 00:37:00.000
I'm sorry.

00:37:00.090 --> 00:37:02.260
Paula, of course I miss you.

00:37:04.490 --> 00:37:11.860
Listen, Paula, Paula, it's just that I don't feel like talking now.

00:37:11.860 --> 00:37:12.800
I'll call you later.

00:37:12.800 --> 00:37:14.020
Don't strain yourself.

00:37:14.530 --> 00:37:16.970
You phone me sometime when you feel more like talking.

00:37:19.290 --> 00:37:21.710
Oh, by the way, I called that Mr. Phillips back.

00:37:22.150 --> 00:37:22.840
Phillips?

00:37:23.410 --> 00:37:25.070
Yes, you know, the man that tried to reach you.

00:37:25.460 --> 00:37:28.180
Well, I'm afraid you'll never know why it was so important that he speak to you.

00:37:28.470 --> 00:37:30.000
His office said he died yesterday.

00:37:42.510 --> 00:37:45.320
so you won't have to bother your little head about him anymore.

00:37:45.520 --> 00:37:46.930
You can just go ahead and have fun.

00:37:48.680 --> 00:37:51.780
Paula, where did he die from? Do you know?

00:37:51.980 --> 00:37:54.480
I suppose he died from whatever people usually die from.

00:37:54.990 --> 00:37:56.490
Well, didn't they tell you? Don't you know?

00:37:56.690 --> 00:37:59.380
What are you getting so excited about? You said you didn't even know the man.

00:38:00.160 --> 00:38:02.880
- Where's his office located? - What difference does it make?

00:38:03.080 --> 00:38:04.880
I told you, the man's dead.

00:38:05.050 --> 00:38:08.200
Paula, will you stop talking and tell me where his office is?

00:38:09.300 --> 00:38:15.720
Alright. It's the Philips Importing and Exporting Company,

00:38:15.800 --> 00:38:17.920
Bradbury Building, Los Angeles.

00:38:18.650 --> 00:38:20.960
- Bradbury Building, Los Angeles. - That's right.

00:38:21.100 --> 00:38:24.740
- This is really a switch. - Listen, if you want to reach me, I'll be in Los Angeles.

00:38:24.940 --> 00:38:27.530
- Are you out of your mind? - I'm sorry, Paula, I've got to hurry.

00:38:27.730 --> 00:38:29.600
Wait a minute, we're in Los Angeles.

00:38:30.320 --> 00:38:32.850
The Allison Hotel. Goodbye, Paula.

00:39:08.320 --> 00:39:10.960
- I'd like to see someone in charge here. - What is it in regard to?

00:39:10.960 --> 00:39:13.800
- It's a personal matter, it's quite urgent. - Perhaps Mr. Halliday can help you.

00:39:13.800 --> 00:39:15.890
- Who's he? - He's our controller.

00:39:15.890 --> 00:39:19.000
- Your name, please? - Bigelow.

00:39:19.000 --> 00:39:21.700
- Mr. Bigelow to see you. - Send him in.

00:39:21.700 --> 00:39:30.000
Go right in, please. That door.

00:39:30.280 --> 00:39:35.190
- How are you, Mr. Halliday? - What can I do for you?

00:39:35.680 --> 00:39:38.160
Mr. Phillips phoned my office several times yesterday.

00:39:38.280 --> 00:39:41.430
- I'd like to find out what it's all about. - Do you know Mr. Phillips died yesterday?

00:39:41.890 --> 00:39:44.150
- Yes, I know. - Well, I don't understand.

00:39:44.860 --> 00:39:46.900
If he phoned you, didn't he tell you what it was about?

00:39:47.580 --> 00:39:50.580
Well, he didn't speak to me. I wasn't in my office at the time.

00:39:50.600 --> 00:39:52.120
And he wouldn't tell my secretary.

00:39:52.570 --> 00:39:54.740
I'm afraid I can't be of much help, Mr. Biglow.

00:39:55.060 --> 00:39:57.300
I have no idea why Mr. Phillips tried to reach you.

00:39:58.040 --> 00:39:59.890
I'm sorry you had to make the trip for nothing.

00:40:00.830 --> 00:40:03.710
- How do you know I made a trip? - I didn't say anything about making a trip.

00:40:03.810 --> 00:40:06.850
I merely said he phoned my office. My office could be here in Los Angeles.

00:40:08.090 --> 00:40:12.420
- Ms. Foster. - Yes?

00:40:12.650 --> 00:40:16.640
Didn't you mention something yesterday about Mr. Phillips speaking with Mr. Bigelow in San Francisco?

00:40:16.660 --> 00:40:18.960
I said that he had phoned Mr. Bigelow's office in Banning,

00:40:19.060 --> 00:40:22.180
but that Mr. Bigelow was staying at the St. Francis Hotel in San Francisco.

00:40:22.190 --> 00:40:24.680
- I'm sorry you misunderstood me. - Do you know why Mr. Phillips called?

00:40:24.780 --> 00:40:26.790
- No, I don't. - All right, thank you, Ms. Foster.

00:40:27.330 --> 00:40:29.880
You can understand that we've been somewhat upset around here.

00:40:30.920 --> 00:40:33.860
Now, if you don't mind...

00:40:33.860 --> 00:40:41.300
Do Mr. Phillips have a wife, family, anyone that could help me?

00:40:41.300 --> 00:40:43.860
You can't intrude on people at a time like this

00:40:43.860 --> 00:40:45.360
just to satisfy some curiosity.

00:40:45.360 --> 00:40:47.860
- It isn't just curiosity. - Then I suggest you wait a week or so.

00:40:47.860 --> 00:40:49.460
- I can't wait. - Well, I'm sorry, you'll have to.

00:40:49.460 --> 00:40:51.060
Well, there's always a phone book.

00:40:51.060 --> 00:40:53.520
You're a pretty aggressive fellow, Big Low.

00:40:53.520 --> 00:40:56.500
Are you quite sure that this is as important as you make it appear to be?

00:40:56.500 --> 00:40:57.980
It's important.

00:40:57.980 --> 00:41:00.000
Mrs. Phillips lives at the Sunset Arms apartment.

00:41:02.170 --> 00:41:08.680
I'd even tell you she's under a strain.

00:41:08.680 --> 00:41:11.140
I suppose you're capable of using a little more tact with her

00:41:11.140 --> 00:41:12.540
than you demonstrated with me.

00:41:12.540 --> 00:41:13.870
I think I can handle it.

00:41:13.870 --> 00:41:16.810
By the way, what was the cause of Mr. Phillips' death?

00:41:16.810 --> 00:41:18.030
Suicide.

00:41:18.030 --> 00:41:20.740
He lived from the balcony of his apartment.

00:41:34.320 --> 00:41:36.700
Come in, Mr. Bigelow.

00:41:41.450 --> 00:41:43.260
Stanley Phillips, Eugene's brother.

00:41:43.460 --> 00:41:47.030
Halliday, you're coming.

00:41:50.300 --> 00:41:52.620
This is my sister-in-law, Mrs. Phillips.

00:41:52.820 --> 00:41:55.830
I'll try to make this as brief as possible, Mrs. Phillips.

00:41:56.030 --> 00:42:00.000
I'm afraid I can't be of any help to you, Mr. Bigelow.

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:02.280
I don't know why my husband wanted to speak to you.

00:42:05.500 --> 00:42:07.520
I think Halliday covered everything.

00:42:09.180 --> 00:42:12.580
Did your husband mention anything about me, Mrs. Phillips?

00:42:13.040 --> 00:42:17.000
No, I can't remember that you mentioned your name.

00:42:26.920 --> 00:42:30.000
I hate to ask you, Mrs. Phillips, but it's important to me.

00:42:31.340 --> 00:42:33.520
Do you know why your husband committed suicide?

00:42:38.510 --> 00:42:43.740
You're not the most diplomatic person in the world.

00:42:44.560 --> 00:42:48.140
- Were you a friend of my brother's? - I never met him.

00:42:54.160 --> 00:42:56.360
My brother was in a jam, a pretty bad jam.

00:42:56.600 --> 00:42:58.370
He was arrested two days ago.

00:42:58.620 --> 00:43:00.000
He sold some iridium to a dealer,

00:43:00.190 --> 00:43:05.960
- It's a very rare metal, very costly. - Anyway, the Iridium turned out to be stolen.

00:43:05.960 --> 00:43:09.330
He was released on bail yesterday, but he faced a pretty stiff prison term.

00:43:09.330 --> 00:43:13.670
- And have committed suicide for less. - Yes, I know. That's how the police feel about it.

00:43:13.670 --> 00:43:15.920
What puzzles me, though, is this crooked deal.

00:43:15.920 --> 00:43:19.230
Knowing Eugene, you wouldn't say he's the type of man to be mixed up in anything like that, would you?

00:43:19.230 --> 00:43:22.280
- I told you, I never met him. - That's right, so you did.

00:43:22.280 --> 00:43:25.630
- Now, what's this all got to do with you, Biglow? - I don't know.

00:43:25.630 --> 00:43:27.770
Let's complain with each other, Biglow.

00:43:27.770 --> 00:43:30.000
Surely you must have some idea why my brother was so desperate to contact him.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.120
- I have no idea. - That's odd.

00:43:32.450 --> 00:43:34.450
Then how could it be of such vital importance to you?

00:43:34.480 --> 00:43:36.480
You seem to know the answer to everything else.

00:43:36.800 --> 00:43:38.460
Maybe you know the answer to that one too.

00:43:38.580 --> 00:43:52.310
I'm here for you to call operator 82 at Banning.

00:43:52.440 --> 00:43:53.360
Oh, thank you.

00:43:53.610 --> 00:43:55.360
Show Mr. Bigelow to room 821.

00:43:55.560 --> 00:43:57.960
Say, would you have the operator put this call through to my room right away?

00:43:58.160 --> 00:43:59.700
- I'll take it up there. - Yes.

00:44:01.020 --> 00:44:04.910
Hello, operator.

00:44:04.910 --> 00:44:06.800
Here, I'll call you if I need anything.

00:44:06.800 --> 00:44:08.290
Thank you, sir.

00:44:08.290 --> 00:44:09.550
Hello, Paula?

00:44:09.550 --> 00:44:13.770
Well, Sinbad, I'd just about given you up for lost.

00:44:13.770 --> 00:44:18.330
Now, do you mind telling me just why you rushed down to Los Angeles?

00:44:18.330 --> 00:44:21.040
I can't explain it to you just now, Paula.

00:44:21.040 --> 00:44:22.480
I just can't explain it.

00:44:22.480 --> 00:44:24.040
What's going on, Frank?

00:44:24.040 --> 00:44:25.580
You don't even sound like yourself.

00:44:25.580 --> 00:44:30.000
Well, I'm just a little tired, Paula.

00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:36.200
- That's all. But I miss you. - Oh, Frank.

00:44:36.200 --> 00:44:40.210
I can't tell you how good it is to hear you say that.

00:44:40.210 --> 00:44:42.810
And here I was worrying that I'd lost my charm.

00:44:42.810 --> 00:44:51.080
- When are you coming home, Frank? - Soon, Pa. I'll be home soon.

00:44:51.080 --> 00:44:54.080
I'll go right out and get myself a permanent, so I'll be pretty when you see me.

00:44:54.080 --> 00:44:58.200
Hey, guess what? I found that Phillips name in your notarial ledger.

00:45:00.480 --> 00:45:02.720
Yes, of all places.

00:45:03.080 --> 00:45:04.920
I remember now, I made the entry myself.

00:45:05.350 --> 00:45:06.910
You had notarized a paper one morning

00:45:06.910 --> 00:45:08.110
before I came to work.

00:45:08.530 --> 00:45:09.590
What kind of paper was it?

00:45:09.950 --> 00:45:12.140
A bill of sale for a George Reynolds

00:45:12.140 --> 00:45:14.320
made out to Eugene Phillips of Los Angeles.

00:45:15.080 --> 00:45:16.100
So you see, I was right.

00:45:16.260 --> 00:45:17.600
We hadn't done any business with Phillips,

00:45:17.680 --> 00:45:18.360
only indirectly.

00:45:18.860 --> 00:45:20.110
What was the bill of sale for?

00:45:20.350 --> 00:45:22.290
A shipment of iridium, whatever that is.

00:45:22.540 --> 00:45:23.020
Iridium?

00:45:23.450 --> 00:45:25.500
You mentioned at the time that this fellow Reynolds

00:45:25.500 --> 00:45:27.470
had made some kind of a deal in Palm Springs

00:45:27.470 --> 00:45:29.550
and he stopped in your office early in the morning

00:45:29.550 --> 00:45:30.000
on his way.

00:45:30.030 --> 00:45:31.410
to have it notarized.

00:45:31.410 --> 00:45:32.940
- Wait a minute.

00:45:32.940 --> 00:45:33.780
Wait a minute, George Reynolds,

00:45:33.780 --> 00:45:36.990
that was about six months ago, wasn't it?

00:45:36.990 --> 00:45:38.290
- That's right, six months ago.

00:45:38.290 --> 00:45:39.130
- Thanks, Paul.

00:45:39.130 --> 00:45:40.280
Oh, goodbye.

00:45:44.220 --> 00:45:47.090
- Hello, operator, get that number back for me.

00:46:09.310 --> 00:46:12.900
- I've got to talk to you, Mrs. Phillips. - Please, go away.

00:46:13.680 --> 00:46:16.200
- I want to be left alone. - But I found out why your husband wanted to see me.

00:46:16.400 --> 00:46:19.400
- It was in connection with a bill of sale. - Come in.

00:46:20.010 --> 00:46:24.610
Thank you. What do you know about a man named George Reynolds?

00:46:25.010 --> 00:46:26.050
- George Reynolds? - Yes.

00:46:26.570 --> 00:46:30.000
- Why, that's the man my husband claims sold in the Iridium. - And what did Reynolds claim?

00:46:30.480 --> 00:46:32.240
- Reynolds disappeared. - Yes.

00:46:32.500 --> 00:46:36.250
About two months ago, my husband was suspicious that something was wrong.

00:46:36.790 --> 00:46:40.560
Since then, he tried in every way to locate Reynolds, but could find no trace of him.

00:46:40.650 --> 00:46:41.450
But I don't get it.

00:46:41.650 --> 00:46:43.450
Your husband could have proved he made a legitimate deal

00:46:43.650 --> 00:46:45.250
by showing the bill of sale he got from Reynolds.

00:46:45.450 --> 00:46:47.650
- And there was a bill of sale? - Yes, yes, of course there was.

00:46:47.850 --> 00:46:50.650
My husband swore there was, but at the time of his arrest,

00:46:50.850 --> 00:46:53.650
he couldn't find it. It was mysteriously missing.

00:46:53.830 --> 00:46:55.470
Well, then, if your husband could have shown proof,

00:46:55.670 --> 00:46:57.870
it would have been George Reynolds who would have faced the prison term.

00:46:58.010 --> 00:47:00.000
Eugene was convinced that Reynolds had stolen

00:47:00.280 --> 00:47:04.040
He was the only one who had reason to eliminate evidence of the transaction.

00:47:04.040 --> 00:47:09.120
Thank you, Mrs. Phillips. Thank you very much. You've been very helpful.

00:47:09.120 --> 00:47:14.840
Oh, if you'd only come sooner, Mr. Bigelow. My husband might be alive today.

00:47:14.840 --> 00:47:29.090
What puzzles me, Mrs. Phillips, is that you haven't asked how I knew there was a bill of sale.

00:47:42.760 --> 00:47:45.890
If Holliday isn't in, he should be back shortly.

00:47:45.990 --> 00:47:47.790
I think you're the one who can help me, Miss Foster.

00:47:47.890 --> 00:47:50.790
Mr. Phillips tried to reach someone else before he called me yesterday, didn't he?

00:47:50.890 --> 00:47:52.190
Why don't you ask Mr. Holliday?

00:47:52.290 --> 00:47:54.290
Obviously, Mr. Holliday wasn't here yesterday,

00:47:54.390 --> 00:47:56.590
or he wouldn't have had to learn from you that Phillips called me.

00:47:56.690 --> 00:47:59.460
And you're the logical person to know who else Phillips called.

00:47:59.560 --> 00:48:00.000
I don't believe that's anything.

00:48:00.200 --> 00:48:03.200
- What's your business, Mr. Bigelow? - Don't think you're confident.

00:48:03.400 --> 00:48:06.000
I know that he tried to reach someone else, but Mrs. Phillips told me.

00:48:06.200 --> 00:48:09.320
You're bluffing, Mr. Bigelow. I don't know what you're after, but you're trying to trick me.

00:48:09.760 --> 00:48:11.520
Mrs. Phillips didn't tell you a thing.

00:48:11.590 --> 00:48:14.470
- How do you know that? - Mrs. Phillips knows nothing about it.

00:48:14.550 --> 00:48:17.380
She doesn't? Why wouldn't she? Wait a minute.

00:48:18.160 --> 00:48:20.160
I was talking about George Reynolds. Who did you think I meant?

00:48:20.360 --> 00:48:21.960
Just who is it that Mrs. Phillips doesn't know about?

00:48:22.160 --> 00:48:24.170
- I told you before, that's none of your business. - All right, young lady.

00:48:24.370 --> 00:48:25.570
I'm going to give it to you straight. Phillips was murdered.

00:48:25.770 --> 00:48:28.570
- Murdered? I don't believe you. - He told me because he needed me to clear him.

00:48:28.770 --> 00:48:30.000
This is innocent.

00:48:30.000 --> 00:48:32.840
Just who are you trying to protect, Ms. Forster?

00:48:32.960 --> 00:48:34.420
Why are you so afraid to tell the truth?

00:48:34.580 --> 00:48:36.940
I'm not protecting anyone. I don't have any more to say.

00:48:37.100 --> 00:48:39.900
Listen to me. This thing is going to explode wide open.

00:48:40.060 --> 00:48:41.940
If you have nothing to hide, you better start talking.

00:48:42.100 --> 00:48:43.860
- Or maybe you are mixed up with us. - No!

00:48:44.140 --> 00:48:45.130
Then come on.

00:48:45.290 --> 00:48:46.970
Mr. Phillips is called Marla Recubian.

00:48:47.030 --> 00:48:48.750
He went to see her yesterday morning.

00:48:48.910 --> 00:48:50.710
- Who's Marla Recubian? - She's a model.

00:48:51.070 --> 00:48:52.790
She and Mr. Phillips used to be quite friendly,

00:48:52.950 --> 00:48:54.550
but he hadn't seen her for quite some time.

00:48:54.710 --> 00:48:56.800
The last couple of months he had been trying to locate her

00:48:56.960 --> 00:48:58.760
and finally learned where she lived yesterday morning.

00:48:58.920 --> 00:49:00.000
When he returned from there,

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.500
He was terribly upset and excited.

00:49:02.600 --> 00:49:04.500
That's when he put in the calls for you.

00:49:04.600 --> 00:49:06.500
When he couldn't reach you, he went home.

00:49:06.600 --> 00:49:08.390
The last time I saw him alive.

00:49:08.470 --> 00:49:11.150
Give me Marla Rakubian's address.

00:49:11.240 --> 00:49:16.870
I don't think Mr. Phillips realized I was aware of his friendship with Marla Rakubian.

00:49:16.930 --> 00:49:19.840
Out of respect for him, I never intended to tell anybody.

00:49:19.850 --> 00:49:23.520
I had no idea that she had anything to do with the trouble he was in.

00:49:23.590 --> 00:49:26.100
I admire your discretion, Miss Foster.

00:49:26.200 --> 00:49:30.000
You know, you must be pretty friendly with Stanley.

00:49:30.000 --> 00:49:33.010
He knew how desperately his brother tried to reach me yesterday

00:49:33.010 --> 00:49:34.330
and he wasn't even here at the time.

00:49:35.000 --> 00:49:37.720
And now you seem to know all about what happened in Mrs. Phillips' apartment.

00:49:41.610 --> 00:49:47.220
Mr. Kubian?

00:49:47.360 --> 00:49:47.660
Yes.

00:49:48.020 --> 00:49:49.540
What do you want?

00:49:49.940 --> 00:49:51.310
Get out of here. I'll call the police.

00:49:51.310 --> 00:49:52.150
Go ahead. Call him.

00:49:53.330 --> 00:49:54.270
Oh, go ahead. Call him.

00:49:54.530 --> 00:49:55.390
Going on a trip, huh?

00:49:56.080 --> 00:49:57.940
Yes. Going away for the weekend.

00:49:58.250 --> 00:50:00.000
Sailing for Buenos Aires tomorrow, some weekend.

00:50:00.560 --> 00:50:02.280
I'll send you a postcard. Now get out of here.

00:50:02.400 --> 00:50:03.360
Who are you going with, George Reynolds?

00:50:03.950 --> 00:50:05.490
Heard of him.

00:50:05.550 --> 00:50:07.130
I suppose you've never heard of Eugene Phillips either.

00:50:07.560 --> 00:50:09.170
Just who are you? What do you want?

00:50:09.210 --> 00:50:10.510
Never mind who I am. Where's Reynolds?

00:50:11.090 --> 00:50:14.140
I told you I don't know him. Now will you get out of here and leave me alone?

00:50:16.340 --> 00:50:21.560
So you never heard of George Reynolds, huh?

00:50:21.830 --> 00:50:24.040
And don't try to tell me that this isn't him because I've seen him.

00:50:24.180 --> 00:50:25.880
If you think you can scare me, you're crazy.

00:50:25.900 --> 00:50:27.490
Look, I know that Phillips came here yesterday.

00:50:27.810 --> 00:50:30.000
And right after he left, he was pushed out of a six-story window.

00:50:30.250 --> 00:50:32.130
Phillips committed suicide.

00:50:32.330 --> 00:50:33.930
Your playmate, Reynolds, murdered Phillips.

00:50:34.130 --> 00:50:35.930
Then he went to San Francisco to get me.

00:50:36.130 --> 00:50:38.130
Because I know about a certain bill of sale.

00:50:38.540 --> 00:50:39.740
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:50:39.940 --> 00:50:41.940
You're in this right up to your pretty little neck.

00:50:42.140 --> 00:50:43.320
I'm not mixed up in anything.

00:50:43.710 --> 00:50:44.650
Get your hands up.

00:50:45.210 --> 00:50:46.210
Drop that picture on the couch.

00:50:46.320 --> 00:50:47.600
Turn around.

00:50:49.790 --> 00:50:52.190
Don't get any ideas because I'm not afraid to use this.

00:50:52.750 --> 00:50:54.210
Give me your wallet.

00:51:00.090 --> 00:51:07.870
- Where's Reynolds? - I don't know. I don't know where he is.

00:51:08.070 --> 00:51:10.950
- Is that what you told Phillips yesterday? - I told him exactly what I'm telling you.

00:51:11.150 --> 00:51:12.350
I haven't heard from him in months.

00:51:12.550 --> 00:51:15.880
Yeah? You're mighty careful of the picture of a man you haven't heard from in months.

00:51:15.970 --> 00:51:19.580
- What does the race stand for? - It was a pet name. Do you mind?

00:51:19.780 --> 00:51:21.780
Well, it sounds very cozy, Miss Recoupian.

00:51:21.840 --> 00:51:24.630
You and Reynolds call each other pet names while you make a sucker out of Phillips.

00:51:24.830 --> 00:51:27.130
- Phillips made the deal because he wanted it. - Yeah?

00:51:27.680 --> 00:51:30.000
I'll bet you you weren't above using what it takes to help me.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:32.210
Who's paying for this trip?

00:51:32.210 --> 00:51:33.930
I am.

00:51:33.930 --> 00:51:35.110
Really?

00:51:35.110 --> 00:51:36.940
A first class trip to Buenos Aires on a model salary

00:51:36.940 --> 00:51:38.940
don't make me laugh.

00:51:38.940 --> 00:51:41.180
Since you and Reynolds aren't seeing each other anymore,

00:51:41.180 --> 00:51:42.180
you don't mind if I keep this to you.

00:51:42.180 --> 00:51:46.930
Were a man, I'd punch your dirty face in.

00:51:46.930 --> 00:51:49.530
I really believe you would.

00:51:49.530 --> 00:51:53.590
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:51:53.590 --> 00:51:55.470
Your tickets.

00:51:55.470 --> 00:51:59.700
Don't be surprised if I'm there to see you off.

00:52:29.180 --> 00:52:30.000
Do you remember taking this picture?

00:52:30.080 --> 00:52:33.120
- George Remmels. - I take pictures, I can't remember them all.

00:52:33.280 --> 00:52:36.480
This gentleman is a friend of his. We have no card on him.

00:52:36.670 --> 00:52:38.070
I don't think we should do that.

00:52:38.200 --> 00:52:40.080
He's willing to pay $20 for it.

00:52:40.560 --> 00:52:42.580
That's the paper we used last year.

00:52:42.730 --> 00:52:45.450
We usually don't give out the information about our clients.

00:52:45.610 --> 00:52:47.790
- I know, you're a lot of high-class guys. - Thank you.

00:52:48.120 --> 00:52:50.920
If anything confidential is against the ethics of our establishment.

00:52:51.080 --> 00:52:53.460
- That's right. Honesty is the best policy. - Of course.

00:52:54.740 --> 00:52:57.220
But in your case, as much as your personal friend of Mr. Remmels...

00:52:57.380 --> 00:52:59.060
- Thanks, I knew you'd come through. - Got it.

00:53:00.540 --> 00:53:03.660
We don't have his address, he must have called for the picture.

00:53:03.740 --> 00:53:05.730
He couldn't have been a good friend of yours.

00:53:05.770 --> 00:53:07.560
His name is not George Reynolds.

00:53:08.170 --> 00:53:09.990
- It isn't. - What is it?

00:53:10.130 --> 00:53:12.560
- It's... - Huh?

00:53:13.370 --> 00:53:18.820
- Oh, it's Raymond Rakubian. - Rakubian?

00:53:19.920 --> 00:53:21.960
What's the news about that?

00:53:22.030 --> 00:53:23.990
The picture is gray, isn't it?

00:53:25.000 --> 00:53:29.120
Yes.

00:56:26.050 --> 00:56:27.940
- Can I get you anything? - No, thanks.

00:56:28.400 --> 00:56:30.000
Do you know this man?

00:56:30.760 --> 00:56:33.800
- No, I don't think so. - Are you sure you've never seen him?

00:56:33.920 --> 00:56:34.870
Quite sure.

00:56:35.420 --> 00:56:37.940
Does the name Raymond Rakubian mean anything to you?

00:56:39.220 --> 00:56:40.600
No, I've never heard of him. Why?

00:56:40.770 --> 00:56:42.770
He also uses the name George Reynolds.

00:56:42.830 --> 00:56:44.220
- This is Reynolds? - That's right.

00:56:44.340 --> 00:56:46.420
- Where can we find him? - That's what I want to know.

00:56:46.830 --> 00:56:49.520
Tell me something, Holiday. You're the controller here.

00:56:49.820 --> 00:56:51.890
How come you didn't know about that bill of sale?

00:56:51.970 --> 00:56:53.770
Phillips made that deal before I came to work here.

00:56:53.890 --> 00:56:55.700
Yeah, but you still keep records, don't you?

00:56:55.710 --> 00:56:57.840
For some reason, which is none of my business.

00:56:57.940 --> 00:57:00.000
Phillips preferred to keep that among his personal papers.

00:57:00.860 --> 00:57:02.480
Now, does that answer your question?

00:57:03.500 --> 00:57:06.000
You came in here today asking for some information that you needed,

00:57:06.100 --> 00:57:08.160
and I tried to be as cooperative as I could.

00:57:08.410 --> 00:57:10.180
But now you're beginning to annoy me.

00:57:10.460 --> 00:57:12.070
So get out before I throw you out.

00:57:16.930 --> 00:57:19.010
You know, you really frighten me.

00:57:51.050 --> 00:57:51.990
He showed up big enough.

00:58:00.640 --> 00:58:02.090
Very cute, aren't you, Bigelow?

00:58:02.090 --> 00:58:03.390
Just very cute.

00:58:03.390 --> 00:58:05.690
Marla didn't lose much time getting a hold of you guys, did she?

00:58:05.690 --> 00:58:06.540
Shut up!

00:58:06.540 --> 00:58:08.040
Let's go, Bigelow.

00:58:08.040 --> 00:58:09.220
Look at him.

00:58:09.220 --> 00:58:10.770
He can't take it.

00:58:10.770 --> 00:58:14.440
Soft in the back.

00:58:14.440 --> 00:58:17.720
You do that again, and I'll kick your face out.

00:58:17.720 --> 00:58:18.820
Lay off, Chester. Cut it out.

00:58:18.820 --> 00:58:23.650
Shut up! Who asked you?

00:58:23.650 --> 00:58:26.330
Better let him answer it. The clerk might know he's in.

00:58:26.330 --> 00:58:28.040
Go ahead, Bigelow.

00:58:35.560 --> 00:58:38.720
Frank, why did you hang up on me? I've been trying to get you for hours.

00:58:39.080 --> 00:58:41.350
I'm sorry, Paula. I was in a hurry.

00:58:41.540 --> 00:58:46.270
Don't be in such a hurry this time. You didn't give me a chance to finish what I had to say.

00:58:46.590 --> 00:58:51.110
I wanted to tell you that McGowan was in hollering his head off because you didn't go over the books.

00:58:51.420 --> 00:58:53.270
Tell McGowan to get another audit.

00:58:53.440 --> 00:58:57.360
Sure. I'll just do that little thing and lose the best paying account we've got.

00:58:57.520 --> 00:59:00.000
Do as I tell you, Paula.

00:59:00.220 --> 00:59:02.650
Frank, are you... Are you drunk?

00:59:02.650 --> 00:59:05.380
Paula, how much have we got in the bank?

00:59:05.380 --> 00:59:08.350
About... $2,200.

00:59:08.350 --> 00:59:10.850
Draw it out tomorrow.

00:59:10.850 --> 00:59:15.290
Sure. Then what do we do? Skip town without paying our bills?

00:59:15.290 --> 00:59:20.240
Forget the bills. You know that coat you always wanted? Buy it.

00:59:20.240 --> 00:59:22.730
You are drunk.

00:59:22.730 --> 00:59:27.900
You know, if I didn't have such a good character, I'd be tempted to take advantage of your intoxicated state, Mr. Bigelow.

00:59:27.900 --> 00:59:29.190
I'm not drunk, Paula.

00:59:30.220 --> 00:59:32.680
Don't tell me that one day away from me can affect you this way.

00:59:32.680 --> 00:59:36.820
- Cut it short. - Paula.

00:59:36.820 --> 00:59:38.870
Yes?

00:59:38.870 --> 00:59:43.030
I'm sorry I... I left you.

00:59:43.030 --> 00:59:46.100
I never realized how much I love you.

00:59:46.100 --> 00:59:54.160
Oh, Frank, Frank, darling, I love you too, so very much.

00:59:54.160 --> 00:59:59.410
Please come home. I miss you terribly.

01:00:05.050 --> 01:00:06.770
I'd just love to let you in at Bigelow.

01:00:06.770 --> 01:00:09.660
Let's go, Chester. This guy's kept us waiting long enough now.

01:00:09.660 --> 01:00:11.160
Walk in front of Bigelow.

01:00:13.080 --> 01:00:14.150
Keep your mouth shut.

01:00:14.150 --> 01:00:19.520
If you so much as look cross-eyed at him, blow the back of your skull out.

01:00:35.660 --> 01:00:37.060
Bigelow's really cute.

01:00:37.330 --> 01:00:39.100
He wanted to get tough with Chester.

01:00:39.370 --> 01:00:40.420
He doesn't know Chester.

01:00:40.650 --> 01:00:41.790
Did you get the picture?

01:00:41.990 --> 01:00:44.590
Don't I always get what Mr. Majak sends me after?

01:00:44.690 --> 01:00:45.680
Majak?

01:00:47.410 --> 01:00:48.600
That's right.

01:00:50.160 --> 01:00:52.760
I'm the dealer who bought the iridium from Phillips.

01:00:53.270 --> 01:00:54.250
I get it.

01:00:54.650 --> 01:00:57.090
You have Rakubian unload stolen stuff on Phillips

01:00:57.290 --> 01:00:59.830
for the help of Marla here, and then you buy it back from him.

01:01:00.090 --> 01:01:02.280
You've made a fool out of Phillips.

01:01:04.360 --> 01:01:05.760
What is it, Mr. Bigelow?

01:01:06.280 --> 01:01:08.900
What is on your mind?

01:01:09.400 --> 01:01:11.110
I'm looking for Raymond Rakubian.

01:01:11.600 --> 01:01:12.100
Why?

01:01:12.990 --> 01:01:16.290
Marla told you everything else, too.

01:01:17.330 --> 01:01:20.580
You don't expect me to believe this conversation.

01:01:21.530 --> 01:01:24.740
So, what is on your mind? I mean, underneath.

01:01:26.160 --> 01:01:29.480
You forced your way into my affairs, and now I want to know why.

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:32.720
I just told you, I'm looking for Raymond Recubian.

01:01:33.080 --> 01:01:36.150
Oh, get cute. I'm just itching to work you over.

01:01:36.830 --> 01:01:39.030
Soft in the belly, can't take it.

01:01:40.540 --> 01:01:41.770
See what I tell you?

01:01:43.700 --> 01:01:56.410
Give that to Chester. I'm going to blow your guts out.

01:01:56.610 --> 01:01:57.390
Easy.

01:01:57.590 --> 01:01:59.440
Way up, Chester, not now.

01:02:02.240 --> 01:02:05.610
Look at him. He's so scared of Chester, he'll talk now.

01:02:06.070 --> 01:02:07.490
He's not afraid, Chester.

01:02:10.300 --> 01:02:12.900
You can tell from a man's eyes when he's afraid.

01:02:14.120 --> 01:02:15.360
Look at his eyes.

01:02:28.760 --> 01:02:29.800
I'm telling you, Majak?

01:02:30.410 --> 01:02:33.650
You better keep him away from me or he's really going to have to use that gun.

01:02:35.430 --> 01:02:36.600
Go away, Chester.

01:02:36.920 --> 01:02:41.410
Please, do what I tell you, my boy.

01:02:42.040 --> 01:02:45.200
Please, and help Dave.

01:02:51.630 --> 01:02:57.390
He's an unfortunate boy.

01:02:58.240 --> 01:02:59.350
He's psychopathic.

01:03:01.600 --> 01:03:04.270
He's unhappy unless he gives pain.

01:03:04.450 --> 01:03:11.980
He likes to see blood. Come with me, Mr. Bigelow.

01:03:17.250 --> 01:03:19.230
Raymond Rokobian was my nephew.

01:03:19.690 --> 01:03:21.610
He could not have tried to kill you.

01:03:21.690 --> 01:03:24.100
He's been dead five months.

01:03:30.540 --> 01:03:33.780
I'm afraid you have been sidetracked.

01:03:33.780 --> 01:03:37.060
Provided it is true that somebody made an attempt on your life.

01:03:37.060 --> 01:03:39.660
Somebody made an attempt again today.

01:03:39.660 --> 01:03:42.500
I had no reason to kill you, believe me.

01:03:42.500 --> 01:03:43.770
What do you mean you had no reason?

01:03:43.770 --> 01:03:46.040
I notarized a certain bill of sale.

01:03:46.040 --> 01:03:50.370
You notarized a bill of sale for Reynolds, not Recubia.

01:03:50.370 --> 01:03:52.170
Now, what I told you was true.

01:03:52.170 --> 01:03:54.070
I had no reason to kill you.

01:03:54.070 --> 01:03:57.390
That's a closet, Mr. Beagle.

01:03:57.390 --> 01:04:00.000
Under other circumstances, you could

01:04:00.320 --> 01:04:08.830
- Now you present a problem. - You know too much, and I'm in danger.

01:04:09.030 --> 01:04:13.180
- Chester! - Suppose I can prove to you that I only want to find the person who tried to kill me.

01:04:13.380 --> 01:04:15.220
I won't cause you any trouble.

01:04:15.510 --> 01:04:19.270
You know I can go to jail for 10 years for this little business?

01:04:19.470 --> 01:04:25.010
10 years? At my age, that's my life. That means my entire life.

01:04:25.210 --> 01:04:29.480
With my life, I do not take chances. I'm sorry, believe me.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:32.290
- Do you want Joe to go with you? - No.

01:04:32.290 --> 01:04:35.710
Just Bigelow and me, and Baby Maester.

01:04:35.710 --> 01:04:38.120
But me, Jane.

01:04:38.120 --> 01:04:41.740
Goodbye, Mr. Bigelow, and forgive me.

01:04:41.740 --> 01:04:44.640
Let's go, Bigelow.

01:04:44.640 --> 01:04:49.680
I guess you won't be there to see me off.

01:05:04.920 --> 01:05:07.320
Tried to make a boop out of me in front of me, Chad.

01:05:07.320 --> 01:05:09.090
You shouldn't have done that, Bigelow.

01:05:09.090 --> 01:05:10.790
I don't like that.

01:05:10.790 --> 01:05:15.400
I'm gonna enjoy this, Bigelow.

01:05:15.400 --> 01:05:18.820
I've done jobs like this before.

01:05:18.820 --> 01:05:21.570
I knocked off guys I could like.

01:05:21.570 --> 01:05:24.450
But I don't like you, Bigelow.

01:05:24.450 --> 01:05:28.390
I never liked that puss of yours from the minute I seen it.

01:05:33.040 --> 01:05:42.520
I'm going to enjoy this.

01:05:42.520 --> 01:05:51.130
Not scared yet, are you, Bigelow?

01:05:51.130 --> 01:05:52.960
But you'll be scared.

01:05:52.960 --> 01:05:54.870
Goodly scared.

01:05:54.870 --> 01:05:57.080
I think I'll give it to you in the belly.

01:05:57.080 --> 01:05:58.130
You don't like it in the belly?

01:06:08.280 --> 01:06:09.640
I'd just love you to try it, Bigelum.

01:06:09.640 --> 01:06:11.040
Why don't you try it?

01:06:11.040 --> 01:06:19.450
You didn't have the nerve, did you, Bigelum?

01:06:19.450 --> 01:06:23.880
I think I'll give it to you right in the belly.

01:06:37.100 --> 01:06:38.420
It's longer when you get it in the belly.

01:06:38.420 --> 01:06:41.330
Nice and slow.

01:06:41.330 --> 01:06:43.930
That's the way I want to see you go big along.

01:06:43.930 --> 01:06:45.910
Nice and slow.

01:09:00.320 --> 01:09:01.980
- Are you all right? - Yes, I'm all right, Paula.

01:09:01.980 --> 01:09:03.740
But what are you doing here? How did you get here?

01:09:03.740 --> 01:09:06.690
Freddy Ross flew me down. I had to come. I had to see you.

01:09:06.690 --> 01:09:09.330
You shouldn't have come, Paula. You shouldn't have.

01:09:09.330 --> 01:09:12.290
What is it, Frank? You're in some kind of trouble. I know it.

01:09:12.290 --> 01:09:15.760
Look at you. Your sight. Your clothes look as if you've slept in them.

01:09:15.760 --> 01:09:18.570
Are you ill? You are. You're feverish.

01:09:18.570 --> 01:09:21.030
I'm all right, Paula, and I'm not in any trouble, believe me.

01:09:21.030 --> 01:09:22.790
You're lying, Frank. Right after I spoke to you,

01:09:22.790 --> 01:09:25.000
I got a phone call from the San Francisco police.

01:09:25.000 --> 01:09:26.420
They asked if I knew where you were.

01:09:26.420 --> 01:09:28.560
- You didn't tell them anything, did you? - Of course not.

01:09:28.560 --> 01:09:30.000
It was the homicide detective that caught me.

01:09:32.680 --> 01:09:36.440
What is it, Frank? If you're in any kind of trouble, you certainly can trust me.

01:09:36.440 --> 01:09:39.240
Look, I'm not in any trouble with the police, Paula, believe me.

01:09:39.240 --> 01:09:41.960
But you can't stay here. You've got to go back to Banning right away.

01:09:41.960 --> 01:09:44.920
No, I won't go, Frank. I won't. I'm staying here with you.

01:09:44.920 --> 01:09:47.000
Paula, it's better that you go back, believe me.

01:09:47.000 --> 01:09:49.360
Why? What's this all about?

01:09:49.360 --> 01:09:54.280
What have you got to do with this Phillips and Reynolds?

01:09:54.280 --> 01:09:57.750
Phillips was murdered.

01:09:57.750 --> 01:10:00.000
What could that possibly have to do with you?

01:10:00.000 --> 01:10:01.460
All you did was notarize a paper.

01:10:01.460 --> 01:10:03.040
You've notarized hundreds of papers.

01:10:03.040 --> 01:10:04.040
I know, I know.

01:10:04.040 --> 01:10:05.880
All I did was notarize one little paper,

01:10:05.880 --> 01:10:08.080
one little paper out of hundreds.

01:10:08.080 --> 01:10:09.500
Frank, you frighten me.

01:10:09.500 --> 01:10:11.400
You don't even act like yourself.

01:10:11.400 --> 01:10:12.700
I know that you're in trouble,

01:10:12.700 --> 01:10:13.900
that something is wrong,

01:10:13.900 --> 01:10:15.780
that you're in serious trouble.

01:10:15.780 --> 01:10:17.440
You frighten me, Frank.

01:10:17.440 --> 01:10:20.110
Oh, don't be frightened, Paula.

01:10:20.110 --> 01:10:21.730
Don't ever be frightened of anything again.

01:10:21.730 --> 01:10:23.010
Will you promise me that?

01:10:23.010 --> 01:10:24.510
I love you so much, darling,

01:10:24.510 --> 01:10:27.280
more than you seem able to understand.

01:10:27.280 --> 01:10:30.000
I never really knew happiness until I loved you.

01:10:30.030 --> 01:10:32.750
Sometimes when I used to be afraid that you weren't sure how you felt,

01:10:32.750 --> 01:10:34.910
I tried to hold back, but I couldn't.

01:10:35.560 --> 01:10:37.480
Losing you would have been losing everything.

01:10:37.480 --> 01:10:39.760
- There would have been nothing left. - Don't, Paula, don't.

01:10:40.460 --> 01:10:41.540
Now I'm afraid again.

01:10:41.540 --> 01:10:42.900
Somehow I feel that I'm going to lose you,

01:10:42.900 --> 01:10:44.380
but there's nothing I can do about it.

01:10:44.380 --> 01:10:47.180
I feel so helpless, you're leaving me out of something.

01:10:47.180 --> 01:10:48.460
Tell me, Frank, what is it?

01:10:48.460 --> 01:10:51.620
Give me a chance to fight back, just give me a chance, please.

01:10:51.620 --> 01:10:55.000
- You do love me, don't you? - Oh, yes, Paula, I love you.

01:10:55.000 --> 01:10:56.920
I never was most certain of anything in my life.

01:10:56.920 --> 01:11:00.000
I wasn't sure before, I was a little blind, I guess, but believe me,

01:11:00.030 --> 01:11:02.930
- Do you understand that, Paula? - I understand.

01:11:03.030 --> 01:11:04.930
A man can be like that, Paula.

01:11:05.030 --> 01:11:07.850
If something has to happen, it can be a big thing or a little thing,

01:11:07.950 --> 01:11:09.850
but it can make him realize how much someone means to him,

01:11:09.950 --> 01:11:11.850
how much he really loves him.

01:11:11.950 --> 01:11:13.850
Oh, and I love you, Paula.

01:11:13.950 --> 01:11:18.190
More than I ever thought it possible to love anyone in the world, I love you.

01:11:18.290 --> 01:11:20.080
Then why won't you tell me about this trouble you're in?

01:11:20.180 --> 01:11:22.080
Why won't you try to let me help you?

01:11:22.180 --> 01:11:26.940
- You can't help me, Paula. - You don't want my help.

01:11:27.040 --> 01:11:30.000
Oh, Paula, there's nothing you can do, will you believe me?

01:11:30.090 --> 01:11:32.280
So, will you please go home, please?

01:11:32.470 --> 01:11:34.710
No, Frank, I won't go.

01:11:35.060 --> 01:11:37.860
I know you're in trouble, I can't leave you like this.

01:11:38.940 --> 01:11:43.530
Paula, wait for me in the lobby of the hotel and I'll be back soon.

01:11:43.730 --> 01:11:46.180
- You're sure? - Yes, Paula, I promise.

01:11:47.780 --> 01:11:50.710
- Is that a new outfit? - Yes.

01:11:50.920 --> 01:11:51.800
It's beautiful.

01:12:01.020 --> 01:12:04.670
- You'll come back to me, Frank. - Yes, Paula, I'll come back.

01:12:04.790 --> 01:12:07.070
Hurry up, darling. I love you.

01:12:07.340 --> 01:12:09.830
I love you, Paula.

01:12:49.450 --> 01:12:51.390
Is Stanley here?

01:12:51.390 --> 01:12:53.730
You sure?

01:12:53.730 --> 01:12:55.390
Get in.

01:12:55.390 --> 01:12:57.260
Get Stanley on the phone.

01:12:57.260 --> 01:12:58.360
Tell him to come over here right away.

01:12:58.360 --> 01:12:59.640
Use any excuse you want.

01:13:00.380 --> 01:13:04.000
- What are you going to do? - What was Stanley going to do when he used me for a clay pigeon?

01:13:04.000 --> 01:13:07.280
- I don't know what you're talking about. - Don't act innocent with me. I fell for that once.

01:13:07.280 --> 01:13:10.220
I don't know what you mean. I told you everything you wanted to know this morning.

01:13:10.220 --> 01:13:14.400
Yeah, you told me just enough so I'd get sidetracked and wouldn't know that Stanley was the one I was after.

01:13:14.400 --> 01:13:17.920
Stanley? Oh no!

01:13:17.920 --> 01:13:20.210
You and Stanley have been together on this from the start.

01:13:20.210 --> 01:13:22.410
Now come on, get on that phone and call him.

01:13:22.410 --> 01:13:24.660
Don't let him know I'm here.

01:13:24.660 --> 01:13:25.540
Speak along.

01:13:36.300 --> 01:13:40.640
It was the poor little widow who did it.

01:13:41.850 --> 01:13:43.810
Mr. Foster found this letter this afternoon.

01:13:44.290 --> 01:13:46.050
It's at my brother's desk at the office.

01:13:46.220 --> 01:13:47.380
It was postmarked two years ago.

01:13:48.440 --> 01:13:52.180
It's not exactly the kind of a letter a married woman gets from a casual friend.

01:13:53.160 --> 01:13:56.690
I'm sure my brother wasn't aware that they were so well acquainted when he hired Halliday.

01:14:00.760 --> 01:14:03.340
- He hasn't felt right since dinner. - Where did he have dinner?

01:14:03.420 --> 01:14:04.620
At Mrs. Phillips' apartment.

01:14:04.700 --> 01:14:08.470
Halliday was there too, and Stanley confronted him with that letter.

01:14:08.550 --> 01:14:10.870
- Do you have anything to drink? - Yes, why?

01:14:10.950 --> 01:14:11.960
How long ago?

01:14:12.040 --> 01:14:13.880
Half an hour ago, just before I came here.

01:14:13.960 --> 01:14:16.360
Miss Forster, get on the phone and call the emergency hospital.

01:14:16.440 --> 01:14:17.960
Have him get an ambulance over here right away.

01:14:18.040 --> 01:14:20.840
- What? - Tell him to prepare a stomach wash for luminous poisoning.

01:14:20.920 --> 01:14:22.920
- For luminous poisoning? - Come on, do what I tell you.

01:14:23.000 --> 01:14:24.800
- He may still have a chance to save his life. - But I...

01:14:24.880 --> 01:14:26.880
Go on!

01:14:32.150 --> 01:14:42.760
George Reynolds, Mrs. Phillips.

01:14:43.220 --> 01:14:45.010
He's been dead for five months.

01:14:45.460 --> 01:14:47.150
Then he didn't steal the bill of sale.

01:14:47.190 --> 01:14:49.270
No, he didn't. But you could have stolen it.

01:14:49.660 --> 01:14:51.130
How dare you!

01:14:51.640 --> 01:14:53.620
You knew who I was when I came here today.

01:14:54.260 --> 01:14:56.440
But you were surprised to see me alive, weren't you?

01:14:56.760 --> 01:14:58.360
But I'm not alive, Mrs. Phillips.

01:14:59.060 --> 01:15:00.000
Sure, I can stand here.

01:15:00.890 --> 01:15:03.780
I can breathe and I can move, but I'm not alive.

01:15:04.220 --> 01:15:07.680
Because I did take that poison and nothing can save me.

01:15:10.980 --> 01:15:12.940
- What are you going to do? - I kill you now, I have nothing to lose.

01:15:13.140 --> 01:15:15.780
No, you've got to listen to me. You've got to give me a chance.

01:15:15.980 --> 01:15:17.350
But I didn't have a chance.

01:15:17.470 --> 01:15:19.670
It was Halliday. Believe me, it was Halliday.

01:15:19.870 --> 01:15:21.990
He made me steal the bill of sale. He planned everything.

01:15:22.190 --> 01:15:24.520
What about this letter? Your husband knew about you and Halliday.

01:15:24.720 --> 01:15:26.840
He found it only yesterday. He accused Halliday.

01:15:27.040 --> 01:15:30.000
They fought and Halliday pushed him over this balcony.

01:15:30.190 --> 01:15:31.870
Why me? Why did he want to kill me?

01:15:31.870 --> 01:15:33.950
Because you could have proved there was a bill of sale,

01:15:33.950 --> 01:15:36.430
that my husband had no reason to commit suicide.

01:15:36.430 --> 01:15:39.190
Holiday was desperate after he killed my husband.

01:15:39.190 --> 01:15:40.910
He found out about the phone calls to you.

01:15:40.910 --> 01:15:43.670
He thought you spoke to him, that you knew enough to involve him.

01:16:00.540 --> 01:16:02.350
Where is he?

01:16:02.350 --> 01:16:04.330
He's at the office.

01:16:04.330 --> 01:16:10.050
This time, you don't want him.

01:16:30.220 --> 01:16:30.680
*music*

01:19:31.240 --> 01:19:33.680
Let's break it up. Let's go.

01:21:32.330 --> 01:21:34.430
was notarize a bill of sale.

01:21:36.620 --> 01:21:38.180
That piece of paper could have proven

01:21:38.180 --> 01:21:40.480
that Phillips didn't commit suicide.

01:21:41.820 --> 01:21:42.600
It was murder.

01:21:43.700 --> 01:21:45.400
And that's why Halliday poisoned me.

01:22:24.960 --> 01:22:28.040
If you go to the Alison's hotel, find Paula Gibson, don't tell her anything.

01:22:28.320 --> 01:22:29.220
Break it to her.

01:22:34.160 --> 01:22:36.050
Shall I make out the report on him, Captain?

01:22:38.190 --> 01:22:39.860
Better make a dead on arrival.
